摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"dsh 内置自动更新插件 — Auto-update for DeepSeek Harness: safe version detection, exit-time apply, health check, auto-rollback & circuit breaker.","id":"gh:1343443264","install_available":true,"language":"JavaScript","name":"dsh-autoupdate","slug":"lc23313/dsh-autoupdate","topics":["dsh","dsh-plugin","dsh-plugins"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"dsh 内置自动更新插件 — Auto-update for DeepSeek Harness: safe version detection, exit-time apply, health che"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"ck, auto-rollback & circuit breaker."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-autoupdate"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"A built-in auto-update plugin for dsh (DeepSeek Harness). It adds a **检查更新 (Check for Updates)** sec"},{"id":"p3s2","text":"tion to the dsh Settings page: one click checks npm for a new `@deepseek-ai/dsh` release, a confirm "},{"id":"p3s3","text":"dialog schedules it, and a **guarded update transaction** — exit-time install, health verification, "},{"id":"p3s4","text":"automatic rollback — does the rest."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"中文文档 (Chinese README)"},{"id":"p5s1","text":"## Highlights"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"- **Settings-page UI (v1.1.0)**: 检查更新 button under Settings → 自动更新; modal shows version info with 确认"},{"id":"p6s2","text":"更新 / 取消, or \"当前已是最新版本，暂无可用更新\"\n- **Manual by default (v1.1.0)**: no silent periodic checks — detectio"},{"id":"p6s3","text":"n runs only on the button click (`autoCheck: true` restores the v1.0.0 periodic mode)\n- **Update cha"},{"id":"p6s4","text":"nnel**: any npm dist-tag (`latest`, `rc`, …)\n- **Exit-time application**: a detached helper waits fo"},{"id":"p6s5","text":"r the dsh process to exit before touching the global install — avoids Windows file locks and survive"},{"id":"p6s6","text":"s even a killed dsh\n- **Targeted install**: resolves the *running* dsh's own npm prefix (from `proce"},{"id":"p6s7","text":"ss.argv[1]`) and installs into it with `--prefix` — immune to multi-Node PATH confusion\n- **Transact"},{"id":"p6s8","text":"ion safety**: exact-version install → dual verification (manifest + actually running the new binary)"},{"id":"p6s9","text":" → automatic rollback to the previous version on any failure\n- **Circuit breaker**: consecutive fail"},{"id":"p6s10","text":"ures degrade `auto → notify → off`; any success restores full automation\n- **Optional profile refres"},{"id":"p6s11","text":"h**: after a CLI update, user plugins in your profiles can be refreshed via `dsh plugin --profile <p"},{"id":"p6s12","text":"> update` (with manifest backup/restore)\n- **Breaking-update survivability**: zero runtime dependenc"},{"id":"p6s13","text":"ies, no dsh internal API calls on the backend; the UI uses only the settings-section slot, a generic"},{"id":"p6s14","text":" RPC channel, and plain same-origin fetch — see docs/COMPATIBILITY.zh.md and docs/UI.zh.md"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"For the local v1.1.3 fix, run `dsh plugin --profile web add ./dsh-autoupdate-1.1.3.tgz` from this pr"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"oject and restart dsh. Check and confirm in Settings → Updates, then exit the **dsh process** (closi"},{"id":"p8s3","text":"ng the browser is insufficient). Wait for `helper-result.json` to report `phase: \"done\"` before rest"},{"id":"p8s4","text":"arting. Automatic application requires a discoverable npm global installation; an unknown prefix is "},{"id":"p8s5","text":"utomatic application requires a discoverable npm global installation; an unknown prefix is rejected."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"Install into any dsh profile through the official plugin channel:"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"Verify it was registered as a profile layer, then restart dsh:"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"By default, open Settings → Updates and click Check for updates. With autoCheck: true, checks run 30"},{"id":"p13s2","text":" seconds after boot and every 6 hours. State and logs live in `$DSH_HOME/plugins-data/dsh-autoupdate"},{"id":"p13s3","text":"/` (default `~/.dsh/`)."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"## Configuration"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"Defaults live in the package's own `cordis.patch.yml`; override them per profile in `~/.dsh/profiles"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"/<name>/cordis.patch.yml` (a user-layer row replaces the row's whole config; omitted keys fall back "},{"id":"p15s3","text":"to schema defaults):"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"| Option                      | Default       | Description                                         "},{"id":"p17s2","text":"                             |"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"| `enabled`                   | `true`        | Master switch; `false` = no-op                      "},{"id":"p18s2","text":"                             |\n| `channel`                   | `\"latest\"`    | npm dist-tag to track"},{"id":"p18s3","text":"; falls back to `latest`                                    |\n| `autoApply`                 | `true`"},{"id":"p18s4","text":"        | `false` = detect + notify only (prints a manual command)                         |\n| `auto"},{"id":"p18s5","text":"Check`                 | `false`       | v1.1.0: `false` = manual mode (Settings button only); `true"},{"id":"p18s6","text":"` = v1.0.0 periodic checks |\n| `checkIntervalMs`           | `21600000`    | Check interval when `au"},{"id":"p18s7","text":"toCheck: true` (6 h; floor 5 min)                         |\n| `startupDelayMs`            | `30000` "},{"id":"p18s8","text":"      | Delay before the first check after boot                                          |\n| `maxCon"},{"id":"p18s9","text":"secutiveFailures`    | `3`           | N failures → `notify`, 2N → `off`                            "},{"id":"p18s10","text":"                    |\n| `cooldownMs`                | `86400000`    | Pause auto-apply after an appl"},{"id":"p18s11","text":"y failure                                          |\n| `npmTimeoutMs`              | `30000`       |"},{"id":"p18s12","text":" Timeout for npm queries                                                          |\n| `installTimeou"},{"id":"p18s13","text":"tMs`          | `300000`      | Timeout for npm install / pnpm update                               "},{"id":"p18s14","text":"             |\n| `npmCommand` / `dshCommand` | `npm` / `dsh` | Command overrides (absolute paths all"},{"id":"p18s15","text":"owed)                                       |\n| `registry`                  | `\"\"`          | npm re"},{"id":"p18s16","text":"gistry override (mirrors)                                                  |\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"## Security & trust"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"Before installing any plugin that can run package installs, you should know exactly what this one do"},{"id":"p20s2","text":"ore installing any plugin that can run package installs, you should know exactly what this one does:"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"- It spawns **only** `npm` (version queries, `npm install -g @deepseek-ai/dsh@<exact version>` into "},{"id":"p21s2","text":"the prefix dsh itself runs from) and, optionally, `dsh plugin --profile <p> update|install` for prof"},{"id":"p21s3","text":"iles that depend on this plugin.\n- It **never** writes to dsh-owned files (`settings.yaml`, `cordis."},{"id":"p21s4","text":"patch.yml`, profile manifests). All state/logs are confined to `$DSH_HOME/plugins-data/dsh-autoupdat"},{"id":"p21s5","text":"e/`.\n- It never reads or transmits credentials; npm runs under your own environment and registry con"},{"id":"p21s6","text":"figuration.\n- Every decision is logged with full detail to `autoupdate.log` — audit it any time.\n- A"},{"id":"p21s7","text":"ll installs pin an **exact** version resolved at check time; rollbacks reinstall the previous exact "},{"id":"p21s8","text":"lls pin an **exact** version resolved at check time; rollbacks reinstall the previous exact version."},{"id":"p22s1","text":"## Known limitations"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"1. **Concurrent dsh instances**: the helper waits only for the arming process; if another instance s"},{"id":"p23s2","text":"till holds locks, npm fails and retries ×3, then defers to the next cycle (circuit breaker counts it"},{"id":"p23s3","text":").\n2. **Long offline periods**: 6 consecutive check failures silence the plugin (`off`); periodic re"},{"id":"p23s4","text":"covery probes resume checks after reconnect; successful checks clear check-failure degradation.\n3. *"},{"id":"p23s5","text":"*One-shot headless runs** may exit before the first check; lower `startupDelayMs` for those workflow"},{"id":"p23s6","text":"ne-shot headless runs** may exit before the first check; lower `startupDelayMs` for those workflows."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
